{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Then the man shall be cleared of iniquity</b> — ונקה has three tagin on the heh, to tell you he is cleared of five iniquities, and they are: the iniquity of a married woman, the iniquity of an unmarried woman, the iniquity of [a man] who did not have relations with her, the iniquity of his sons, the iniquity of his daughters." "<b>her iniquity</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other in Nedarim, ונשא את עונה. As stated in Sotah: let the husband not worry to say 'I caused her death,' rather she shall bear her iniquity. And specifically here, but in Nedarim, where her husband could have annulled [her vow] and did not annul it — he shall bear her iniquity."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:13.551367320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}